<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch unemployment seen slightly lower.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch unemployment seen slightly lower.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank economists expect a slight fall in average unemployment for the three months to October, compared with the three months to September.</p>
<p>August-October unemployment data is due to be published on Tuesday morning. Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p>GMT---Date---Period---Indicator---------Consensus--Range----Pvs</p>
<p>0830  19/11  Aug-Oct  Unemployment NSA  438,000    430-445  441</p>
<p>0830  19/11  Aug-Oct  Unemployment SA   439,000    430-447  441</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, ING, Generale Bank, MeesPierson, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Kelly, Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
